 from 1010 \u2192 883 with max_wait = 600 exists; only 1 node reached (the source itself), and zero paths enumerated.\n\n**Why it fails structurally:** Node 1010 has exactly 1 event in the whole window (step_03, step_18), and it is *incoming* \u2014 1429 \u2192 1010 (step_08: zero out-neighbours; step_12: 1 event v\u2192u, 0 u\u2192v). A node that never transmits cannot seed a cascade.\n\n**Not a max_wait artefact (step_04):** Even with no waiting constraint at all, 1010 reaches only itself. The 2-hop neighbourhood of 1010 is a tiny 5-node component {380, 605, 1010, 1429, 1542} (step_07), disjoint from 883's neighbourhood {1038, 1209, ...} (step_09) except for a shared static contact of 1542/1209 \u2014 and even the relay 1429 cannot reach 883 in time (step_11).\n\n**Confounder controls:** the window is busy (6,477 events, 1,922 active nodes \u2014 step_02) and contains an active hub 1209 with 11 partners (step_13) that *does* reach 883 promptly at t=73318 (step_17). So the target is live and reachable in general; activity volume and target popularity would naively suggest a cascade, but no influence route originates at 1010 (step_16: 1010 cannot even reach the hub 1209). Activity of the involved nodes is spread across the window (step_15), so the failure is not a sampling gap.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_20982933\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1010, 883, 1429, 1209, 1038],\n  \"window\": [51317, 89717],\n  \"confidence\": 0.94,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_18\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_17\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"Node 1010 participates in exactly one interaction in [51317,89717], and it is inbound (1429->1010), so it has no outgoing event that could start a cascade. Time-respecting search with max_wait=600 reaches only 1010 itself, and even with unlimited waiting 1010 reaches nothing, since its component {380,605,1010,1429,1542} is separate from 883's neighbourhood {1038,1209,...}; the candidate relay 1429 also fails to reach 883 in time. Confounders are controlled: the window is densely active, 883 is contacted promptly by the hub 1209 at t=73318, and activity is spread throughout the window - yet none of that influence originates from 1010.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 57555, "total_output_tokens": 4664, "total_tokens": 62219, "total_latency_ms": 67822, "llm_calls": 8, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}